Forms and polynomial covers in many variables

The manuscript is by Yijie Diao and Lena Wurzinger.

Third-party Lean sources and dependencies

- formalization/Vendor/Wooley contains the nested efficient congruencing proof
  port from S. McColm's Lean monorepo. The source pin, per-file provenance,
  port patch, and MIT No Attribution license accompany the source.
- formalization/Birch/WeylLinearExponential.lean contains an adaptation of
  OpenAI's SquareDifference circle-distance and phase-bound arguments.
  Its source header gives the exact revision. The Apache 2.0 license text is
  in formalization/LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.
- Mathlib and its dependencies are obtained through the pinned Lake manifest
  and carry their respective licenses.

The listed license grants apply to their respective third-party source.
For terms on the manuscript and original Birch code, consult the rights holders.
